soptools (0.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sopwin GUI: reorganize menus into File, Procedure, View, and Help.
  * sopwin GUI: add project Open/Save/Revert and SOP Load with keyboard shortcuts.
  * sopwin GUI: persist workflow position and step state under
    .config/sopwin/<sopname>.conf; write shell logs to
    .config/sopwin/<sopname>/<id>.log.
  * sopwin GUI: improve workflow graph layout, edge routing, arrows, and
    auto-scroll to the current step.
  * sopwin GUI: fix graph pane hide/detach unsplitting the main window by mistake.
  * sopwin GUI: fix Toggle Graph (F2) and Toggle Loggings (Ctrl+L) accelerator handling.
  * sopwin GUI: pane detach icons toggle attach/detach state; detached log window
    includes attach control.
  * sopwin GUI: Help shortcuts use a structured key/description layout; About shows
    an application icon; License uses a read-only scrollable text box.
  * sopwin GUI: treat each branch column as one object (bbox ports); column-to-column
    uses a single edge; nodes fan in/out inside the column.
  * sopwin GUI: wrap edges go right-down-left-past-row-start-down-right into the next
    row; keep left-edge pan stable on resize (wrapping only).
  * sopwin GUI: widen horizontal gaps around branch columns for bend/arrow clearance.
  * sopwin GUI: auto-scroll only when the running step changes and leaves the viewport;
    node click previews content without scrolling.
  * sopwin GUI: show step id in the info header on preview and current step view.
  * sopwin GUI: place content between toolbar and status bar; add canvas border and
    viewport clip so graph paint cannot escape the canvas (fix ResetClip clearing
    the outer clip).
  * sop_model: use zero-padded unique step ids (for example 000sh, 020gpt).

